      "writtenOn": "2024-11-14T07:34:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As I explained in ticket 3083710: Reading of Chinese Id card | https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/system/nfc/+/3083710\nThis is an arbitrary value; it does not come from the ST NFCC. The FW will return \"unknown protocol, frame RF, poll B\" if a Chinese Id card is detected. For simplification, we translate that to a dedicated protocol value. This value is only used inside the system/nfc code, the JNI will see \"unknown protocol, frame RF, type B\", and it is also what will be broadcasted.",
      "parentUuid": "dfc362c3_6d920d8f",
